{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfaBYM5Wp2mdAaEo26gD6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`just spec-check` now runs in the pre-commit hook, before `just check`. The first commit was rejected, and after restructuring the spec the second one went through as `6753e0d`.\n\n1. **Hook:** `.githooks/pre-commit` now runs `just spec-check` and then `just check`. I ran `just install-hooks`, so `core.hooksPath` is `.githooks`.\n2. **First commit failed:** the hook stopped at `docs/specs/SPEC.v1-todo-list-cli-mvp.md:45` and no commit was created. The checker only reports the first problem in each file, so I read its source to get the full set of rules:\n   - `**Implementation Details:**` must sit on a line by itself, **after** `**Acceptance Criteria:**`. The spec had it before the criteria in M1–M4.\n   - Every criterion must be a one-line `- [ ]` / `- [x]` checkbox. M3 had one criterion wrapped onto a second line.\n   - The box is `[x]` only when the milestone is `IMPLEMENTED` or `✅ DONE`, otherwise `[ ]`.\n3. **Spec fixed:** in every milestone I moved the criteria above the details and put the details label on its own line. I joined the wrapped criterion onto one line and added the boxes: `[x]` for M1–M4, `[ ]` for M5–M8. I checked the diff and no wording changed; text was only moved and reformatted.\n4. **Second commit passed:** `just spec-check` exits 0 and `just check` passed with 20/20 tests and 0 warnings. The commit includes the hook, the spec and the prompt-log lines the hook appended to `docs/PROMPTS.md`.\n\nThings you should know:\n- **Setup outside the repo:** sbt and git failed here until I changed some settings, and none of this is committed. For sbt, I pointed it at the `../.cache` sbt/coursier directories and moved its runtime directory (`XDG_RUNTIME_DIR`) to `/tmp`. The `run` script's own fallback to that cache never kicks in because `SBT_OPTS` is already set in your environment. On a normal machine the hook should work as is.\n- **The refine skill doesn't teach the new format:** its Format section doesn't mention checkboxes or that criteria come before details. Specs written from it would likely fail the new hook. That's the \"altered skills\" part of the lesson, and I left it alone because the prompt only asked for the hook and the spec fix.\n- **Uncommitted leftover:** the untracked `.claude/agents/` directory was already there and is still uncommitted."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1360,"cache_read_input_tokens":51144,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1360},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"79c03cc7-8d90-432c-8452-4631ad9ae47f","uuid":"e13f05b4-eca0-4b1b-8c1a-4bb61574d8fc","timestamp":"2026-09-30T19:33:25.973Z","request_id":"req_011CfaBYLiw8vApMHuTmsSJx"}
